  {
    "chunk_id": "npnf-works/gregory-nazianzen-oration-01#GregNaz.Or1.2",
    "work_id": "npnf-works/gregory-nazianzen-oration-01",
    "canonical_ref": "GregNaz.Or1.2",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "On Easter and His Reluctance.",
    "chunk_index": 2,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 362,
    "date_range": [
      361,
      363
    ],
    "date_confidence": "approximate",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "npnf-works/gregory-nazianzen-oration-01#GregNaz.Or1.3.s1",
    "work_id": "npnf-works/gregory-nazianzen-oration-01",
    "canonical_ref": "GregNaz.Or1.3.s1",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "I. It is the Day of the Resurrection, and my Beginning has good auspices. Let us then keep the Festival with splendour, and let us embrace one another.",
    "chunk_index": 3,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 362,
    "date_range": [
      361,
      363
    ],
    "date_confidence": "approximate",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "npnf-works/gregory-nazianzen-oration-01#GregNaz.Or1.3.s2",
    "work_id": "npnf-works/gregory-nazianzen-oration-01",
    "canonical_ref": "GregNaz.Or1.3.s2",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "Let us say Brethren, even to those who hate us; much more to those who have done or suffered aught out of love for us. Let us forgive all offences for the Resurrection’s sake:",
    "chunk_index": 4,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 362,
    "date_range": [
      361,
      363
    ],
    "date_confidence": "approximate",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "npnf-works/gregory-nazianzen-oration-01#GregNaz.Or1.3.s3",
    "work_id": "npnf-works/gregory-nazianzen-oration-01",
    "canonical_ref": "GregNaz.Or1.3.s3",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "let us give one another pardon, I for the noble tyranny which I have suffered (for I can now call it noble);",
    "chunk_index": 5,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 362,
    "date_range": [
      361,
      363
    ],
    "date_confidence": "approximate",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "npnf-works/gregory-nazianzen-oration-01#GregNaz.Or1.3.s4",
    "work_id": "npnf-works/gregory-nazianzen-oration-01",
    "canonical_ref": "GregNaz.Or1.3.s4",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "and you who exercised it, if you had cause to blame my tardiness; for perhaps this tardiness may be more precious in God’s sight than the haste of others.",
    "chunk_index": 6,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 362,
    "date_range": [
      361,
      363
    ],
    "date_confidence": "approximate",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "npnf-works/gregory-nazianzen-oration-01#GregNaz.Or1.3.s5",
    "work_id": "npnf-works/gregory-nazianzen-oration-01",
    "canonical_ref": "GregNaz.Or1.3.s5",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "For it is a good thing even to hold back from God for a little while, as did the great Moses of old, and Jeremiah later on;",
    "chunk_index": 7,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 362,
    "date_range": [
      361,
      363
    ],
    "date_confidence": "approximate",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "npnf-works/gregory-nazianzen-oration-01#GregNaz.Or1.3.s6",
    "work_id": "npnf-works/gregory-nazianzen-oration-01",
    "canonical_ref": "GregNaz.Or1.3.s6",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "and then to run readily to Him when He calls, as did Aaron and Isaiah, so only both be done in a dutiful spirit;—the former because of his own want of strength; the latter because of the Might of Him That calleth.",
    "chunk_index": 8,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 362,
    "date_range": [
      361,
      363
    ],
    "date_confidence": "approximate",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "npnf-works/gregory-nazianzen-oration-01#GregNaz.Or1.4.s1",
    "work_id": "npnf-works/gregory-nazianzen-oration-01",
    "canonical_ref": "GregNaz.Or1.4.s1",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "II. A Mystery anointed me; I withdrew a little while at a Mystery, as much as was needful to examine myself;",
    "chunk_index": 9,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 362,
    "date_range": [
      361,
      363
    ],
    "date_confidence": "approximate",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "npnf-works/gregory-nazianzen-oration-01#GregNaz.Or1.4.s2",
    "work_id": "npnf-works/gregory-nazianzen-oration-01",
    "canonical_ref": "GregNaz.Or1.4.s2",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "now I come in with a Mystery, bringing with me the Day as a good defender of my cowardice and weakness; that He Who to-day rose again from the dead may renew me also by His Spirit;",
    "chunk_index": 10,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 362,
    "date_range": [
      361,
      363
    ],
    "date_confidence": "approximate",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "npnf-works/gregory-nazianzen-oration-01#GregNaz.Or1.4.s3",
    "work_id": "npnf-works/gregory-nazianzen-oration-01",
    "canonical_ref": "GregNaz.Or1.4.s3",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "and, clothing me with the new Man, may give me to His New Creation, to those who are begotten after God, as a good modeller and teacher for Christ, willingly both dying with Him and rising again with Him.",
    "chunk_index": 11,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 362,
    "date_range": [
      361,
      363
    ],
    "date_confidence": "approximate",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "npnf-works/gregory-nazianzen-oration-01#GregNaz.Or1.5.s1",
    "work_id": "npnf-works/gregory-nazianzen-oration-01",
    "canonical_ref": "GregNaz.Or1.5.s1",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "III. Yesterday the Lamb was slain and the door-posts were anointed, and Egypt bewailed her Firstborn, and the Destroyer passed us over, and the Seal was dreadful and reverend, and we were walled in with the Precious Blood.",
    "chunk_index": 12,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 362,
    "date_range": [
      361,
      363
    ],
    "date_confidence": "approximate",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "npnf-works/gregory-nazianzen-oration-01#GregNaz.Or1.5.s2",
    "work_id": "npnf-works/gregory-nazianzen-oration-01",
    "canonical_ref": "GregNaz.Or1.5.s2",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "To-day we have clean escaped from Egypt and from Pharaoh; and there is none to hinder us from keeping a Feast to the Lord our God—the Feast of our Departure;",
    "chunk_index": 13,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 362,
    "date_range": [
      361,
      363
    ],
    "date_confidence": "approximate",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "npnf-works/gregory-nazianzen-oration-01#GregNaz.Or1.5.s3",
    "work_id": "npnf-works/gregory-nazianzen-oration-01",
    "canonical_ref": "GregNaz.Or1.5.s3",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "or from celebrating that Feast, not in the old leaven of malice and wickedness, but in the unleavened bread of sincerity and truth, carrying with us nothing of ungodly and Egyptian leaven.",
    "chunk_index": 14,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 362,
    "date_range": [
      361,
      363
    ],
    "date_confidence": "approximate",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "npnf-works/gregory-nazianzen-oration-01#GregNaz.Or1.6.s1",
    "work_id": "npnf-works/gregory-nazianzen-oration-01",
    "canonical_ref": "GregNaz.Or1.6.s1",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "IV. Yesterday I was crucified with Him; today I am glorified with Him; yesterday I died with Him; to-day I am quickened with Him; yesterday I was buried with Him; to-day I rise with Him.",
    "chunk_index": 15,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 362,
    "date_range": [
      361,
      363
    ],
    "date_confidence": "approximate",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "npnf-works/gregory-nazianzen-oration-01#GregNaz.Or1.6.s2",
    "work_id": "npnf-works/gregory-nazianzen-oration-01",
    "canonical_ref": "GregNaz.Or1.6.s2",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "But let us offer to Him Who suffered and rose again for us—you will think perhaps that I am going to say gold, or silver, or woven work or transparent and costly stones,",
    "chunk_index": 16,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 362,
    "date_range": [
      361,
      363
    ],
    "date_confidence": "approximate",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "npnf-works/gregory-nazianzen-oration-01#GregNaz.Or1.6.s3",
    "work_id": "npnf-works/gregory-nazianzen-oration-01",
    "canonical_ref": "GregNaz.Or1.6.s3",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "the mere passing material of earth, that remains here below, and is for the most part always possessed by bad men, slaves of the world and of the Prince of the world.",
    "chunk_index": 17,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 362,
    "date_range": [
      361,
      363
    ],
    "date_confidence": "approximate",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "npnf-works/gregory-nazianzen-oration-01#GregNaz.Or1.6.s4",
    "work_id": "npnf-works/gregory-nazianzen-oration-01",
    "canonical_ref": "GregNaz.Or1.6.s4",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "Let us offer ourselves, the possession most precious to God, and most fitting; let us give back to the Image what is made after the Image.",
    "chunk_index": 18,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 362,
    "date_range": [
      361,
      363
    ],
    "date_confidence": "approximate",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "npnf-works/gregory-nazianzen-oration-01#GregNaz.Or1.6.s5",
    "work_id": "npnf-works/gregory-nazianzen-oration-01",
    "canonical_ref": "GregNaz.Or1.6.s5",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "Let us recognize our Dignity; let us honour our Archetype; let us know the power of the Mystery, and for what Christ died.",
    "chunk_index": 19,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 362,
    "date_range": [
      361,
      363
    ],
    "date_confidence": "approximate",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "npnf-works/gregory-nazianzen-oration-01#GregNaz.Or1.7.s1",
    "work_id": "npnf-works/gregory-nazianzen-oration-01",
    "canonical_ref": "GregNaz.Or1.7.s1",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "V. Let us become like Christ, since Christ became like us. Let us become God’s for His sake, since He for ours became Man.",
    "chunk_index": 20,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 362,
    "date_range": [
      361,
      363
    ],
    "date_confidence": "approximate",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "npnf-works/gregory-nazianzen-oration-01#GregNaz.Or1.7.s2",
    "work_id": "npnf-works/gregory-nazianzen-oration-01",
    "canonical_ref": "GregNaz.Or1.7.s2",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "He assumed the worse that He might give us the better; He became poor that we through His poverty might be rich; He took upon Him the form of a servant that we might receive back our liberty;",
    "chunk_index": 21,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 362,
    "date_range": [
      361,
      363
    ],
    "date_confidence": "approximate",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "npnf-works/gregory-nazianzen-oration-01#GregNaz.Or1.7.s3",
    "work_id": "npnf-works/gregory-nazianzen-oration-01",
    "canonical_ref": "GregNaz.Or1.7.s3",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "He came down that we might be exalted; He was tempted that we might conquer; He was dishonoured that He might glorify us;",
    "chunk_index": 22,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 362,
    "date_range": [
      361,
      363
    ],
    "date_confidence": "approximate",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "npnf-works/gregory-nazianzen-oration-01#GregNaz.Or1.7.s4",
    "work_id": "npnf-works/gregory-nazianzen-oration-01",
    "canonical_ref": "GregNaz.Or1.7.s4",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "He died that He might save us; He ascended that He might draw to Himself us, who were lying low in the Fall of sin.",
    "chunk_index": 23,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 362,
    "date_range": [
      361,
      363
    ],
    "date_confidence": "approximate",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "npnf-works/gregory-nazianzen-oration-01#GregNaz.Or1.7.s5",
    "work_id": "npnf-works/gregory-nazianzen-oration-01",
    "canonical_ref": "GregNaz.Or1.7.s5",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "Let us give all, offer all, to Him Who gave Himself a Ransom and a Reconciliation for us. But one can give nothing like oneself, understanding the Mystery, and becoming for His sake all that He became for ours.",
    "chunk_index": 24,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 362,
    "date_range": [
      361,
      363
    ],
    "date_confidence": "approximate",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "npnf-works/gregory-nazianzen-oration-01#GregNaz.Or1.8.s1",
    "work_id": "npnf-works/gregory-nazianzen-oration-01",
    "canonical_ref": "GregNaz.Or1.8.s1",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "VI. As you see, He offers you a Shepherd; for this is what your Good Shepherd, who lays down his life for his sheep, is hoping and praying for, and he asks from you his subjects;",
    "chunk_index": 25,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 362,
    "date_range": [
      361,
      363
    ],
    "date_confidence": "approximate",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "npnf-works/gregory-nazianzen-oration-01#GregNaz.Or1.8.s2",
    "work_id": "npnf-works/gregory-nazianzen-oration-01",
    "canonical_ref": "GregNaz.Or1.8.s2",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "and he gives you himself double instead of single, and makes the staff of his old age a staff for your spirit.",
    "chunk_index": 26,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 362,
    "date_range": [
      361,
      363
    ],
    "date_confidence": "approximate",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "npnf-works/gregory-nazianzen-oration-01#GregNaz.Or1.8.s3",
    "work_id": "npnf-works/gregory-nazianzen-oration-01",
    "canonical_ref": "GregNaz.Or1.8.s3",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "And he adds to the inanimate temple a living one; to that exceedingly beautiful and heavenly shrine, this poor and small one, yet to him of great value, and built too with much sweat and many labours.",
    "chunk_index": 27,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 362,
    "date_range": [
      361,
      363
    ],
    "date_confidence": "approximate",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "npnf-works/gregory-nazianzen-oration-01#GregNaz.Or1.8.s4",
    "work_id": "npnf-works/gregory-nazianzen-oration-01",
    "canonical_ref": "GregNaz.Or1.8.s4",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "Would that I could say it is worthy of his labours. And he places at your disposal all that belongs to him (O great generosity!—or it would be truer to say, O fatherly love!)",
    "chunk_index": 28,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 362,
    "date_range": [
      361,
      363
    ],
    "date_confidence": "approximate",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "npnf-works/gregory-nazianzen-oration-01#GregNaz.Or1.8.s5",
    "work_id": "npnf-works/gregory-nazianzen-oration-01",
    "canonical_ref": "GregNaz.Or1.8.s5",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "his hoar hairs, his youth, the temple, the high priest, the testator, the heir, the discourses which you were longing for;",
    "chunk_index": 29,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 362,
    "date_range": [
      361,
      363
    ],
    "date_confidence": "approximate",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "npnf-works/gregory-nazianzen-oration-01#GregNaz.Or1.8.s6",
    "work_id": "npnf-works/gregory-nazianzen-oration-01",
    "canonical_ref": "GregNaz.Or1.8.s6",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "and of these not such as are vain and poured out into the air, and which reach no further than the outward ear;",
    "chunk_index": 30,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 362,
    "date_range": [
      361,
      363
    ],
    "date_confidence": "approximate",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "npnf-works/gregory-nazianzen-oration-01#GregNaz.Or1.8.s7",
    "work_id": "npnf-works/gregory-nazianzen-oration-01",
    "canonical_ref": "GregNaz.Or1.8.s7",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "but those which the Spirit writes and engraves on tables of stone, or of flesh, not merely superficially graven, nor easily to be rubbed off, but marked very deep, not with ink, but with grace.",
    "chunk_index": 31,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 362,
    "date_range": [
      361,
      363
    ],
    "date_confidence": "approximate",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "npnf-works/gregory-nazianzen-oration-01#GregNaz.Or1.9.s1",
    "work_id": "npnf-works/gregory-nazianzen-oration-01",
    "canonical_ref": "GregNaz.Or1.9.s1",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "VII. These are the gifts given you by this august Abraham, this honourable and reverend Head, this Patriarch, this Restingplace of all good,",
    "chunk_index": 32,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 362,
    "date_range": [
      361,
      363
    ],
    "date_confidence": "approximate",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "npnf-works/gregory-nazianzen-oration-01#GregNaz.Or1.9.s2",
    "work_id": "npnf-works/gregory-nazianzen-oration-01",
